# RESILIENT-313 — the persistent farmer runner. The farmer (scripts/coord/farmer.sh,
# RESILIENT-068) is the un-killable control-plane tender that writes the heartbeat
# the worker binary gates on (RESILIENT-069). It is a single-TICK script; nothing
# on helsinki ever scheduled it. The fleet was kept alive only by a fragile,
# hand-installed *transient* `chump-farmer-bridge` unit — this repo-declared
# service+timer retires that hack. Paired with chump-farmer.timer (~every 30s,
# well under the 120s heartbeat-freshness threshold). Runs the wrapper
# (chump-farmer-run.sh) which sources providers.env, sweeps stale leases, and
# refreshes the oauth mtime before each tick.
# Path defaults target the primary node (helsinki, root).
[Unit]
Description=Chump farmer tick — keep the worker-gate heartbeat fresh so the fleet never darks out (RESILIENT-313)
After=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
Environment=HOME=/root
# Source ALL ~/.chump/*.env (export-format creds + config) in the unit's ExecStart
# — the same pattern chump-pr-lander.service uses — BEFORE handing off to the
# wrapper, so the organ's env is loaded even if the wrapper's own source path ever
# regresses. Sourcing the WHOLE *.env glob (not just providers.env) is load-bearing:
# the free-tier provider config (openrouter/deepseek) lives in node.env, and with
# only providers.env sourced, auth-status.sh finds no Anthropic token, falls through
# to a failing Anthropic probe, and returns a FALSE AUTH_DEAD — so the farmer
# withholds the heartbeat and the worker gates itself off, even though a valid
# free-tier provider is configured. VERIFIED: auth-status.sh with all *.env sourced
# returns "AUTH ✓ OK — free-tier provider live (openrouter)". The wrapper then sets
# HOME/PATH, sweeps stale leases, refreshes oauth mtime, and execs one farmer tick
# (which writes ~/.chump/farmer-heartbeat unconditionally at tick start — the file
# the worker gate reads). Non-login shell (-c) so the host-rewriter's injected
# Environment=PATH (run-user's ~/.cargo/bin) is authoritative on every host, not
# reset by a login profile. The host-rewriter turns /root into the run-user's home,
# so the glob resolves to the run-user's ~/.chump on every host. Kept short so it
# always completes well inside the 30s timer cadence.
ExecStart=/bin/bash -c 'set -a; for e in /root/.chump/*.env; do source "$e" 2>/dev/null; done; set +a; exec /root/Projects/chump/scripts/dispatch/chump-farmer-run.sh'
TimeoutStartSec=120
